options.explanation:
$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\dfrac{1}{2y^3}\right]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\dfrac{1}{2}y^{-3}\right]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2}(-3)y^{-4}\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{3}{2y^4}\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}
\end{align}$

Now let's plug $\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\dfrac{1}{2y^3}}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=-\dfrac{3}{2y^4}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{3}{2y^4}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{1}{2y^3}}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{3}{4y^7}
\end{align}$

hints.content:
Finally, let's plug $\blueD{x=-2}$ and $\maroonD{y=1}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\left.-\dfrac{3}{4\maroonD y^7}\right\rvert_{(\blueD{-2},\maroonD{1})}&=-\dfrac{3}{4(\maroonD{1})^7}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{3}{4}
\end{align}$

(Notice that the expression for $\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ only depends on $\maroonD y$ so there was no need to plug $\blueD{x=-2}$.)
